qt-rsync (0.2.0-0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * 0.2.0: refreshed README and KDE-theme screenshots; screenshots, icon and
    desktop entry live in resources/; obsolete Actions labels renamed to
    Decisions; directory decision filters and directory-aware Items counts;
    overview Files row, size-based Share, collapsed folder rows and totals
    that match the root row; overview rebuild keeps sort and folded totals;
    go-jump overview icon; folders absent from one side stay blank there;
    excluding items keeps the cursor on the next visible row after the last
    excluded item, or the previous row, and never uses stale row positions;
    the root row has no exclude checkbox; overview folders can be excluded,
    restored and filtered from Space or their context menu; completion sounds
    now play on comparison and synchronization completion; restored qpy
    keyboard navigation (Home/End, Ctrl+Up/Down, Left/Right); decision-filter
    checkboxes support Ctrl+click and their context menu; action filters hide
    unrelated directories and count only visible folders; sync progress comes
    from rsync counters, the journal keeps only summaries, the comparison
    becomes stale after sync with a root-row marker, Ctrl+Tab layout cycling
    works again, startup options are validated, compare progress is live and
    batched, external tool placeholders are supported, journal lines are
    timestamped, decision filtering and overview building are much faster,
    destination metadata runs after the dry run without overlapping rsync
    passes, journal commands are neutral, tooltips are informative, sizes
    scale to MiB/GiB, decisions and the overview update incrementally, log
    paths and inverted clicks are fixed, directories can become Source or
    Destination, sync starts disabled, modified profiles prompt to be saved
    (Save / Save As... / Don't Save), external tools and remote diff staging
    are ported, all settings are plain text with no base64 or qpy import,
    folding repaints all panes, profiles are listed by recent use, no qpy
    import code remains, log clearing is confirmed, operation buttons start
    disabled, sync can re-compare automatically, progress is in the status
    bar and the command preview is a temporary journal entry, menu chevrons
    point down, the overview keeps its width across layouts, the toolbar is
    reordered, buttons own their left-click menus, swap stays in the top row
    and location changes mark the comparison stale, tooltips keep a uniform
    250 ms delay and the Decisions header has borders; the
    comparison stale, and
    timings report real wall-clock values;
    example profile installed under
    /usr/share/doc/qt-rsync/examples.

 -- Eugene San (eugenesan) <eugenesan@gmail.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:40:00 -0700

qt-rsync (0.1.0-0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * 0.1.0: first pure Qt 6/C++ release. Complete port of qpy-rsync's
    comparison, decision, plan, verification, synchronization, profile,
    settings and filter workflows, with KDE/Breeze dark-theme parity,
    unchanged-item inventory, three compare layouts, a full synchronization
    confirmation dialog and the qpy-style profile/filter editors.

 -- Eugene San (eugenesan) <eugenesan@gmail.com>  Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0700
